      "step_number": 1,
      "text": "Step 1: To find the integer roots of the polynomial \\(x^4 + 5x^3 + 9x^2 - x - 14 = 0\\), we can use the Rational Root Theorem, which states that any rational root, expressed as a fraction \\(\\frac{p}{q}\\), must have \\(p\\) as a factor of the constant term (here, -14) and \\(q\\) as a factor of the leading coefficient (here, 1).",
